Game Description
Tower Ascent is a 2D top-down action-adventure inspired by classic titles like The Legend of Zelda. The world is a single vertical tower with eight floors. Each floor is its own combat arena ending in a boss fight, and every boss, when defeated, surrenders a unique relic that the player carries up the tower.

Core Gameplay & Interface
The player controls a stick-figure protagonist in a top-down combat arena. Controls are twin-stick style: WASD/Arrow keys move the body, the mouse cursor aims, the left mouse button swings melee (no stamina cost), and the right mouse button fires a ranged bolt (costs stamina; independent cooldowns so you can weave both while kiting). F3 drinks a Stamina Potion after it has been unlocked on Floor 1 (short cooldown). Space dashes once the Dash Boots are unlocked on Floor 4. Enemies are driven into the arena by the tower; the player must defeat the floor's boss to spawn the exit portal.

Tower Progression
- The tower has eight floors, from Floor 1 (Slime Pit) through Floor 8 (Lich Summit).
- Each floor has exactly one boss. When the boss dies it drops a floor key and a unique reward.
- Stepping into the exit portal after picking up both drops advances to the next floor. Rewards stack for the final confrontation.
- Defeating the Tower Lich on Floor 8 ends the run with a Victory screen.

Floor Rewards
1. Slime King — Stamina Potion (F3 heal / stamina, cooldown).
2. Skeleton Lord — Iron Sword (+25% melee and ranged damage).
3. Fire Warden — Firebolt Rune (upgrades right-click bolt).
4. Shadow Knight — Dash Boots (Space to dash).
5. Storm Titan — Vitality Charm (+35 max HP).
6. Frost Matriarch — Grit Band (+12 stamina regen / sec).
7. Iron Colossus — Predator Charm (+15% damage).
8. Tower Lich — Tower Amulet (+50% damage, +50 max HP).

Key UI Elements
Player Status (Top-Left): portrait, HP and stamina bars, level.
Tower Progress (Top-Center): "Floor X / 8", floor and boss names, boss HP bar when alive.
Minimap (Top-Right): schematic; blue = player, red = boss, yellow = exit; Esc opens pause.
Inventory (Bottom-Left): item grid; hot hints LMB / RMB / F3 with green pulse while the corresponding input is held in combat; potion cooldown overlay on F3.
Pause: Esc or the Esc button on the minimap.
